    <main>
      <section class="competitions-intro">
        <div class="intro-content">
          <h2>SkillsUSA Competitions</h2>
          <p>
            SkillsUSA competitions provide students with the opportunity to demonstrate the technical
            and professional skills they've learned in their career and technical programs. From
            carpentry and culinary arts to information technology and healthcare, our competitions
            span diverse industries and skill levels.
          </p>
          <p>
            Competitors are evaluated on technical knowledge, craftsmanship, professionalism, and
            teamwork. Winners advance through regional, state, and national levels, with the best
            students competing at the SkillsUSA National Leadership and Skills Conference.
          </p>
          <p>
            Whether you're a first-time competitor or a veteran of the stage, SkillsUSA competitions
            offer a platform to shine and prepare for career success.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="pdf-section">
        <div class="pdf-container">
          <h2>Competition Guidelines & Rules</h2>
          <p>Download the official competition guidelines and rules for this year:</p>
          <div class="pdf-download">
            <a href="/pdfs/competition-guidelines.pdf" class="pdf-link" download>
              Download Competition Guidelines (PDF)
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="pdf-note">
            If the PDF file is not available, please contact us for more information about specific
            competition rules and requirements.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="competitions-content">
        <h2 class="competitions-title">Competition Levels</h2>
        <div class="competitions-grid">
          <div class="competition-card">
            <h3>Local Competitions</h3>
            <p>
              Compete at the school level to advance to regional and state competitions. Build
              experience and connections with other skilled students.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="competition-card">
            <h3>State Championships</h3>
            <p>
              Winners from regional competitions advance to the state championships where the best
              of the best compete for top honors and advancement to nationals.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="competition-card">
            <h3>National Conference</h3>
            <p>
              The ultimate competition experience. Top competitors from all states gather at the
              SkillsUSA National Leadership and Skills Conference.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="competitions-info">
        <div class="info-card">
          <h3>Getting Started</h3>
          <p>
            Interested in competing? Talk to your teacher or advisor about which competition aligns
            with your skills and interests.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="info-card">
          <h3>Preparation</h3>
          <p>
            Work with your advisor to prepare for competition day. Study the technical standards,
            practice your skills, and familiarize yourself with the judging criteria to maximize
            your chances of success.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
